#!/bin/sh
# Foreman MCP sidecar shim. Finds bun even under launchd's restricted PATH and runs the bundled
# stdio server. Unlike the hook shim this fails loudly (stderr, exit 1): Claude then shows the
# server as failed instead of silently lacking the tools.
ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." 2>/dev/null && pwd)" || exit 1
SERVER="$ROOT/dist/mcp.js"
[ -f "$SERVER" ] || { echo "foreman-mcp: $SERVER missing; run 'bun run build:plugin'" >&2; exit 1; }
for c in "$FOREMAN_BUN" "$HOME/.bun/bin/bun" /opt/homebrew/bin/bun /usr/local/bin/bun; do
  if [ -n "$c" ] && [ -x "$c" ]; then exec "$c" "$SERVER" "$@"; fi
done
BUN="$(command -v bun 2>/dev/null)" && [ -n "$BUN" ] && exec "$BUN" "$SERVER" "$@"
echo "foreman-mcp: bun not found" >&2
exit 1
